      "auto_visible": false,
      "show_progress_bar": false,
      "narration": "Let's assume we already have a trained model. It has seen lots of dogs and cats and figured out which clues help tell them apart. To keep things simple, let's say it only looks for two things: floppy ears and a long snout. It has also learned how much each clue should count. Each saved setting is called a weight. Those weights stay fixed so that any change in the answer comes from the new photo, not from changing the rules.",
