      "narration": "In our photo, the ears look quite floppy: seven out of ten. That is not a seventy-percent dog answer; it only measures this clue. The model passes that clue through the ear weight, times zero point five. In everyday terms, the weight turns the clue down. Seven tenths becomes a push of zero point three five toward dog. The snout works the same way. It measures four out of ten, and its weight is zero point five five. That creates a second push: zero point two two toward dog.",
