    {
      "id": "friendlier_scale",
      "duration": "40s",
      "layout": {"type": "grid", "columns": 1, "rows": 1, "gap": "small"},
      "auto_visible": false,
      "show_progress_bar": false,
      "narration": "Zero point five seven does not mean fifty-seven percent. It is an internal score, not a probability. The model passes that score through a function called a sigmoid. Its S-shaped curve puts a score of zero in the middle at fifty percent. Positive scores move up the curve; negative scores move down. A score of zero point five seven lands at about sixty-four percent. This change of scale matters because a percentage is easier to interpret. The evidence has not changed; only the scale has.",
